analysis:
Examined three changes.

1) scripts/ci-component-paths.py full_run (base 131-137, head 131-135). Pull requests into master no longer force a full run; they now select components from the merge-base diff, the same way dev PRs do. Master pushes still select every component (head 133-134), and so does workflow_dispatch (head 140). classify() still forces all components when a COMMON CI file changes (head 110-111). Docs-only paths still skip (head 108). The release lane runs its own build and SDK qualification (provider-release.md head 581-584), so narrower PR CI does not bypass any signing or qualification gate shown here.

2) scripts/ci-tested-tree.py: only metadata was supplied. The file_changes excerpt adds `ci-tested-tree-<tree>-p/c/m` records. These let a master push of a squash merge skip testing when a prior same-repo, successful, same-workflow run tested an identical git root tree. An identical tree implies identical workflow files and sources, so reuse seems sound in principle. However, I could not see the validation code that integration must check:
- that tree records come only from same-repo runs, not forks;
- that run conclusion and workflow path are checked;
- that p/c/m coverage must cover every component the push would run;
- how the tree hash is computed.
This affects the CI gate, not release signing.

3) docs/operations/provider-release.md dev-branch lane (head 497-547). Dev releases are now coalesced on a 6-hour schedule plus manual workflow_dispatch on refs/heads/dev, instead of running on every push. The gate job runs on ubuntu without secrets or contents: write. The source gate (master's verify-source) accepts a current-head dispatch for environment dev only. Branch rulesets are described as requiring reviewed merge commits and signed commits on dev, with limited ref writers. Under those conditions, dispatch only builds reviewed dev HEAD with the same Developer ID signature. This trust rests on the external rulesets and on verify-source, which are not in the supplied source.

The remaining sections (signing key lifetime, cluster runtime facts, certificates, recovery) are unchanged per the range map. No threat-model asset or boundary (TB-002, TB-011, A-011, A-017) is weakened by the visible evidence. No findings.
